WEBVTT

00:00:17.710 --> 00:00:20.830
Long time no see, Fujitani Youichi!

00:00:21.850 --> 00:00:23.180
I've been waiting for you.

00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:26.300
Hey!

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:28.340
Don't you ignore me! What's wrong with you?!

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:29.860
Listen closely!

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:32.560
I'm going to beat you this time!

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:35.590
It's time I finally settled this long-standing feud!

00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:41.220
You may not have realized, but I'm not the same man I was!

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:43.980
You'll show me!

00:00:44.420 --> 00:00:46.480
You mean "I'll show you."

00:00:52.580 --> 00:00:55.070
Golden Week finally starts tomorrow.

00:00:55.570 --> 00:01:00.650
Now, I don't think anybody here is actually
thinking about having a nice, relaxing break.

00:01:00.650 --> 00:01:02.830
What? We're not getting a break?

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:04.500
Of course not.

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:08.710
How could we waste a whole day where you don't even have to go to school?

00:01:10.220 --> 00:01:14.290
Since you'll finally be able to focus on practice, I've decided to take a new initiative.

00:01:14.290 --> 00:01:15.470
What is it?

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:17.720
Combined practice.

00:01:19.310 --> 00:01:24.980
I'll gather other Olympic hopefuls from around Japan to practice with us.

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:29.640
Normally, Fujitani would be the only
one from MDC who could participate,

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:33.990
but you all were allowed to join too because we'll be the ones hosting.

00:01:33.990 --> 00:01:35.510
Good luck.

00:03:02.070 --> 00:03:04.450
See what no one else has ever seen

00:03:18.010 --> 00:03:22.070
Hey, do you know who these great divers are?

00:03:22.070 --> 00:03:23.800
Do you?

00:03:24.500 --> 00:03:25.620
You could say that.

00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:30.320
Probably divers who are going to enter the Asian qualifiers this fall.

00:03:30.320 --> 00:03:34.910
Of course, our Youichi is one of them.

00:03:34.910 --> 00:03:37.820
How do you know all this anyway?

00:03:38.120 --> 00:03:40.920
I've got my own sources.

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:44.940
After all, athletes these days need information in order to compete.

00:03:44.940 --> 00:03:47.610
You know you followed us up here, right?

00:03:47.610 --> 00:03:49.450
You can't do 10 meters yet, Sacchin.

00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:55.950
I keep forgetting because of your punky attitude,
but you're still in elementary school.

00:03:56.870 --> 00:03:58.480
Until the end of the year.

00:03:58.480 --> 00:04:01.350
Watch out, because I'm going to overtake you soon!

00:04:02.980 --> 00:04:09.210
Isn't it exciting that divers on Youichi's level are going to come here from all over Japan?

00:04:09.210 --> 00:04:15.730
I mean, we're going to practice together,
but it'll be more like them showing us how outclassed we are.

00:04:16.120 --> 00:04:18.820
But you know what they say about the 50 meter sprint:

00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:22.030
You run a better time if you race with someone fast.

00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:28.580
So if we practice with great divers, I bet we'll get better too!

00:04:28.580 --> 00:04:33.000
If that's all it took to be better,
then that would've happened already.

00:04:33.770 --> 00:04:37.000
I mean, we've dove with Youichi all this time.

00:04:38.010 --> 00:04:39.290
You've got a point.

00:04:41.940 --> 00:04:44.520
But I'm still looking forward to it.

00:04:44.520 --> 00:04:47.510
I can't believe we get to practice with such amazing people.

00:04:48.550 --> 00:04:51.520
You're never not positive, are you?

00:04:52.510 --> 00:04:53.700
What?

00:04:53.700 --> 00:04:55.160
It's nothing.

00:05:02.860 --> 00:05:05.030
<i>Man, I'm getting so excited.</i>

00:05:10.280 --> 00:05:11.800
See you later, Tomo!

00:05:11.800 --> 00:05:13.120
See you tomorrow!

00:05:26.900 --> 00:05:28.090
I'm home.

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:35.680
You're back.

00:05:35.680 --> 00:05:36.390
Yeah.

00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:38.470
So...

00:05:39.530 --> 00:05:41.370
You're practicing during Golden Week too?

00:05:41.370 --> 00:05:42.400
Yeah.

00:05:43.020 --> 00:05:47.080
We're having a combined practice with divers from other swimming clubs.

00:05:47.720 --> 00:05:48.660
Every day?

00:05:49.330 --> 00:05:51.330
You're not even going to have one day off?

00:05:51.330 --> 00:05:52.090
Yeah.

00:05:52.920 --> 00:05:55.280
Well, good luck.

00:05:55.280 --> 00:05:56.660
What?

00:05:56.970 --> 00:05:58.120
You're not gonna make a comment?

00:06:00.050 --> 00:06:02.670
Why would I do that?

00:06:12.170 --> 00:06:13.180
Morning!

00:06:14.110 --> 00:06:14.930
You're here early.

00:06:15.690 --> 00:06:16.830
Yeah.

00:06:16.830 --> 00:06:18.440
Is it just you?

00:06:20.780 --> 00:06:23.940
Oh, Okitsu's here too.

00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:30.450
I wonder how long he's going to be like that.

00:06:30.780 --> 00:06:32.370
You're telling me.

00:06:32.370 --> 00:06:33.810
He's a stubborn one for sure.

00:06:33.810 --> 00:06:36.950
But he's got the power to draw you in.

00:06:36.950 --> 00:06:38.750
Something about that style of his.

00:06:44.080 --> 00:06:46.020
All right, gather up.

00:06:48.190 --> 00:06:50.970
Here are the members you'll be practicing with starting today.

00:06:51.280 --> 00:06:51.860
Uh, um—

00:06:51.860 --> 00:06:53.910
I'm here from Fukushima Rainbow.

00:06:53.910 --> 00:06:56.230
My name's Tsuji Toshihiko. Nice to meet you.

00:06:56.230 --> 00:06:56.570
I'm—

00:06:56.570 --> 00:06:57.250
Yo!

00:06:57.250 --> 00:07:00.370
I'm from Splash Osaka. The name's Hirayama Jirou.

00:07:00.370 --> 00:07:00.850
My—

00:07:00.850 --> 00:07:04.400
And I'm the brave soldier from Ibaraki Spirits.

00:07:07.290 --> 00:07:08.990
I'm Yamada Atsuhiko.

00:07:09.440 --> 00:07:12.490
<i>Wow, everyone has such strong personalities.</i>

00:07:12.870 --> 00:07:17.240
I've imposed a challenge on myself for this practice.

00:07:17.710 --> 00:07:18.730
And that is...

00:07:20.390 --> 00:07:23.250
Fujitani Youichi, I'm taking you down!

00:07:23.250 --> 00:07:26.450
What? He's leading off with a take down notice?

00:07:26.450 --> 00:07:29.050
You hear me, Fujitani Youichi?

00:07:29.050 --> 00:07:30.760
I see you're still stupid.

00:07:30.760 --> 00:07:34.580
I wonder how long you'll be able
to keep up that attitude of yours.

00:07:34.580 --> 00:07:35.910
For eternity.

00:07:36.710 --> 00:07:38.090
You little...

00:07:38.090 --> 00:07:41.550
You're going to bow to my greatness one of these days.

00:07:41.550 --> 00:07:45.150
How about you start us off, Yamada?

00:07:46.520 --> 00:07:47.900
Be happy to.

00:07:48.650 --> 00:07:49.490
Behold!

00:07:51.690 --> 00:07:55.130
So pink! It's too bright and vivid!

00:07:55.130 --> 00:07:57.410
Ibaraki Spirits' Yamada Atsuhiko.

00:07:58.020 --> 00:07:59.410
His nickname is Pinky.

00:08:00.090 --> 00:08:01.410
That fits him perfectly.

00:08:01.910 --> 00:08:04.410
Burn this image into your mind.

00:08:04.410 --> 00:08:07.930
I'll send you to hell with my diving.

00:08:08.420 --> 00:08:11.240
All right, and we'll send one more person up there.

00:08:11.240 --> 00:08:12.790
Um...

00:08:12.790 --> 00:08:13.940
Who were you again?

00:08:14.690 --> 00:08:16.680
I'm Matsuno from Mare Tokushima.

00:08:25.940 --> 00:08:27.740
The pink is so bright.

00:08:27.740 --> 00:08:30.440
He may be stupid, but he's a good diver.

00:08:31.550 --> 00:08:33.200
That's really nice form.

00:08:33.830 --> 00:08:36.430
He used to take classical ballet.

00:08:36.430 --> 00:08:39.200
You can see his focus extend to his fingertips.

00:08:39.740 --> 00:08:41.450
He also has a good sense of rhythm.

00:08:42.110 --> 00:08:46.710
He has strength, flexibility, and nice proportions.

00:08:52.470 --> 00:08:54.660
Everything he has is better than me.

00:08:54.660 --> 00:09:01.030
Actually, you might even argue that he has more raw talent than Japan's best diver, Teramoto Ken'ichirou.

00:09:01.030 --> 00:09:05.630
Then why does someone like that want to take you down so badly?

00:09:05.630 --> 00:09:07.860
Because he can't beat me in competitions.

00:09:08.670 --> 00:09:09.680
That's right.

00:09:09.680 --> 00:09:12.700
He even loses competitions he's guaranteed to win.

00:09:12.700 --> 00:09:14.360
Even in the last one...

00:09:25.720 --> 00:09:28.350
I remember him now!

00:09:30.170 --> 00:09:33.380
He was too focused on the thought of winning and choked under the pressure.

00:09:38.780 --> 00:09:41.510
He's way too conscious of Fujitani.

00:09:41.900 --> 00:09:46.520
So whether he's winning or losing,
his nerves end up causing him to self-destruct.

00:09:46.940 --> 00:09:51.220
As long as he's under Fujitani's curse, he'll never be able to win, right?

00:09:51.220 --> 00:09:52.940
Don't ask me.

00:09:52.940 --> 00:09:54.670
That's true.

00:09:55.930 --> 00:09:58.820
People call him Fire Jirou.

00:09:58.820 --> 00:10:00.290
Fire?

00:10:00.290 --> 00:10:06.150
If I told you his nickname comes from his intense drive
to always attempt dives with high degrees of difficulty,

00:10:12.580 --> 00:10:17.100
I'd be lying because he's never
pulled off a big move successfully.

00:10:17.100 --> 00:10:21.050
He keeps failing and failing, hitting the water hard.

00:10:21.850 --> 00:10:26.060
By the end of a competition, his body is bright red like fire.

00:10:26.520 --> 00:10:30.060
And that's where his nickname Fire Jirou actually comes from.

00:10:32.050 --> 00:10:34.320
What about him?

00:10:34.880 --> 00:10:36.820
What's his name again?

00:10:37.630 --> 00:10:40.570
Oh, I remember. Mare Tokushima's Matsuno.

00:10:41.120 --> 00:10:44.280
If I'm remembering right,
he dominated in high school last year,

00:10:44.280 --> 00:10:48.330
and he came in second behind Teramoto, the guy most likely to make the Olympics.

00:10:48.700 --> 00:10:51.310
His consistent performance is his strong point, but...

00:10:51.310 --> 00:10:54.090
There's nothing particularly good or bad.

00:10:54.610 --> 00:10:57.200
Nothing about me is special. I'm so boring.

00:10:57.200 --> 00:10:58.670
I'm like air.

00:10:58.670 --> 00:10:59.840
Nobody sees me.

00:10:59.840 --> 00:11:01.840
He's negative and doesn't leave an impression.

00:11:04.350 --> 00:11:06.770
What is Tsuji like?

00:11:06.770 --> 00:11:10.100
He used to be a gymnast.

00:11:10.900 --> 00:11:14.570
He dedicates his training to mastering the standards.

00:11:14.570 --> 00:11:18.910
For example, he would replace a pike for a tuck without adding rotations,

00:11:18.910 --> 00:11:21.990
and then polish the move to perfection, limiting any chances for mistakes.

00:11:22.630 --> 00:11:25.990
Is everyone trying to make it to the Olympics?

00:11:26.580 --> 00:11:27.610
Of course they are.

00:11:35.660 --> 00:11:37.760
Pull your body in tighter.

00:11:41.980 --> 00:11:43.760
Bring your shins up to your chest.

00:11:44.350 --> 00:11:45.290
Do it again.

00:11:46.000 --> 00:11:47.600
Who is she?

00:11:47.600 --> 00:11:49.430
That's our new coach.

00:11:49.430 --> 00:11:51.520
We can see that.

00:11:51.940 --> 00:11:53.350
You had a good coach join.

00:11:53.350 --> 00:11:56.770
I'm scared you're not going to give us a chance to catch up to you, Fujitani.

00:11:57.570 --> 00:11:59.530
You don't sound like you're joking.

00:12:22.950 --> 00:12:24.590
Who was that?

00:12:24.590 --> 00:12:26.860
That's our new guy.

00:12:26.860 --> 00:12:29.430
That's not what we're asking for.

00:12:38.800 --> 00:12:40.260
I get it.

00:12:40.260 --> 00:12:41.320
What?

00:12:41.320 --> 00:12:43.130
What are you challenging?

00:12:43.130 --> 00:12:44.480
Challenging?

00:12:44.480 --> 00:12:47.480
You're challenging yourself to protect something, right?

00:12:47.480 --> 00:12:49.960
Or is it to break something down?

00:12:52.770 --> 00:12:53.460
It's nothing.

00:12:53.970 --> 00:12:55.600
I've got my reasons too!

00:12:55.600 --> 00:12:58.690
I think that diving is about landing big moves!

00:12:59.320 --> 00:13:00.160
I don't care.

00:13:00.160 --> 00:13:02.090
Don't you agree?!

00:13:02.090 --> 00:13:04.760
I see your splashes haven't gotten better.

00:13:04.760 --> 00:13:06.000
I'm done for the day.

00:13:06.000 --> 00:13:07.100
Why?

00:13:07.100 --> 00:13:09.030
There are too many people.

00:13:09.030 --> 00:13:12.400
Does that mean it's too hard to practice together?

00:13:12.400 --> 00:13:14.990
Or should I say, you're too scared?

00:13:15.810 --> 00:13:20.150
If you want to stand on the same start line as them,
you're going to need a clean entry.

00:13:20.150 --> 00:13:21.610
Whatever.

00:13:21.610 --> 00:13:23.760
And don't lump me in with them.

00:13:37.700 --> 00:13:41.090
Pinky is challenging Fujitani again.

00:13:41.090 --> 00:13:41.880
I see.

00:13:42.260 --> 00:13:43.790
And unsurprisingly...

00:13:44.890 --> 00:13:45.630
he loses again.

00:13:46.350 --> 00:13:48.630
Is he always like that?

00:13:48.630 --> 00:13:50.390
Yeah, mostly.

00:13:50.850 --> 00:13:55.270
Pinky wanted to at least beat Fujitani out of the pool,

00:13:56.150 --> 00:13:57.390
so he challenged him to foot races,

00:13:58.090 --> 00:14:00.020
who could stay in the sauna longer,

00:14:00.700 --> 00:14:02.020
weight lifting,

00:14:02.870 --> 00:14:03.780
arm wrestling,

00:14:04.800 --> 00:14:06.030
and even thumb wrestling.

00:14:06.510 --> 00:14:09.110
I think he's lost sight of what he's fighting for.

00:14:09.110 --> 00:14:10.910
But he can never win.

00:14:11.290 --> 00:14:12.920
Not even once.

00:14:12.920 --> 00:14:14.660
Really?

00:14:15.170 --> 00:14:21.420
I think Pinky cares more about beating Fujitani than winning any meet.

00:14:22.380 --> 00:14:25.550
Why does he care so much about Youichi?

00:14:25.550 --> 00:14:30.180
Fujitani Youichi

00:14:25.550 --> 00:14:30.180
Yamada Atsuhiko

00:14:26.180 --> 00:14:30.180
It's probably because he was the
first obstacle he had to overcome.

00:14:30.680 --> 00:14:32.930
He's been like that since elementary school.

00:14:33.430 --> 00:14:35.430
He's never beaten Fujitani.

00:14:35.820 --> 00:14:37.430
Not even once.

00:14:37.430 --> 00:14:39.190
Not in the water or on land.

00:14:39.590 --> 00:14:40.780
Wait!

00:14:40.780 --> 00:14:43.940
This isn't over, Fujitani Youichi!

00:14:44.250 --> 00:14:46.340
But Fujitani isn't much better.

00:14:46.340 --> 00:14:49.700
He could've let him win at least once on land.

00:14:50.010 --> 00:14:53.030
He never does, though.

00:14:53.030 --> 00:14:54.450
Why's that?

00:14:54.760 --> 00:14:58.460
Because Fujitani always strives for
perfection with everything he does.

00:14:58.880 --> 00:15:01.710
And he never lets his emotions get the best of him.

00:15:13.450 --> 00:15:16.490
That was perfect, um...

00:15:16.490 --> 00:15:18.360
I'm Matsuno with Tokushima.

00:15:18.360 --> 00:15:21.790
Oh, are you trying to make me feel better?

00:15:21.790 --> 00:15:23.730
Since I'm so plain?

00:15:23.730 --> 00:15:25.900
No, not at all!

00:15:25.900 --> 00:15:28.590
It was a perfect performance without any mistakes.

00:15:28.590 --> 00:15:33.240
Well, my performance is basically about limiting mistakes.

00:15:33.620 --> 00:15:39.230
While Fujitani and Pinky's performances are
about adding impressive moves for the judges.

00:15:39.230 --> 00:15:41.500
But I don't have that.

00:15:42.300 --> 00:15:44.420
That's why I can never go up in the rankings.

00:15:45.240 --> 00:15:47.500
I'll forever be second place.

00:15:48.260 --> 00:15:50.400
What's wrong with second place?

00:15:50.400 --> 00:15:53.010
Just try to imagine it.

00:15:53.440 --> 00:15:59.050
Would you be happy if the person you had feelings for told you that they liked you the second most?

00:15:59.050 --> 00:16:00.270
Well, that's...

00:16:00.880 --> 00:16:04.270
That's what being forever second place means.

00:16:05.030 --> 00:16:06.270
I see.

00:16:08.880 --> 00:16:11.520
Fujitani is amazing.

00:16:11.520 --> 00:16:13.500
All right, you're up next, Sakai.

00:16:14.160 --> 00:16:15.410
Three-and-a-half, okay?

00:16:51.160 --> 00:16:52.690
You need to bring it in tighter.

00:16:53.230 --> 00:16:55.590
You have to focus all the way down to your fingertips.

00:16:56.460 --> 00:16:57.070
Yes, ma'am.

00:16:57.450 --> 00:16:58.380
That was almost there.

00:16:58.380 --> 00:17:00.080
You're right.

00:17:07.330 --> 00:17:08.490
Hey.

00:17:09.360 --> 00:17:10.910
Are you going for a three-and-a-half?

00:17:10.910 --> 00:17:13.340
Yes, but I haven't been able to do it yet.

00:17:13.750 --> 00:17:16.330
Did that coach tell you to do it?

00:17:16.330 --> 00:17:17.340
Yes.

00:17:17.340 --> 00:17:20.080
Trying a three-and-a-half in junior high?

00:17:20.080 --> 00:17:22.070
That's really impressive.

00:17:22.700 --> 00:17:25.420
I see that you're the same type as Fujitani...

00:17:25.420 --> 00:17:26.600
Oh, I'm nothing like that!

00:17:26.960 --> 00:17:29.260
He's got promise.

00:17:30.500 --> 00:17:31.360
Really?

00:17:31.760 --> 00:17:34.370
He's got Fujitani's seal of approval, huh?

00:17:47.940 --> 00:17:49.380
Fujitani Youichi!

00:17:49.920 --> 00:17:54.380
The next time I see you will be at
the qualifiers for the Beijing camp.

00:17:54.380 --> 00:17:56.500
That is where you'll meet your end.

00:17:56.500 --> 00:17:57.670
You got that?

00:17:58.330 --> 00:17:59.150
Some space, please.

00:18:00.760 --> 00:18:05.430
In any case, I shall be the one in Beijing, shaking hands with pandas.

00:18:06.770 --> 00:18:08.970
Pandas are cute, aren't they?

00:18:08.970 --> 00:18:10.840
I want to shake hands with one too.

00:18:10.840 --> 00:18:14.360
My soul is burning up like a great ball of fire!

00:18:14.360 --> 00:18:15.780
Well, I look forward—

00:18:15.780 --> 00:18:21.780
Thanks for coming today, Yamada, Hirayama, Tsuji, and...

00:18:23.800 --> 00:18:25.120
It's Matsuno.

00:18:25.120 --> 00:18:26.290
Sorry, sorry.

00:18:26.290 --> 00:18:29.210
It's not your fault.

00:18:29.210 --> 00:18:31.500
I'm so quiet and nobody ever notices me...

00:18:39.300 --> 00:18:41.150
You've gotten better.

00:18:41.150 --> 00:18:42.520
Are you able to tell?

00:18:42.520 --> 00:18:43.260
Yes!

00:18:44.000 --> 00:18:46.140
You're just one step away.

00:18:46.140 --> 00:18:47.520
You can do it.

00:18:47.520 --> 00:18:48.470
Yes, ma'am.

00:18:50.770 --> 00:18:52.030
Coach.

00:18:54.130 --> 00:18:56.530
Please teach us how to do a three-and-a-half too.

00:18:58.840 --> 00:19:00.530
It's too hard for you two.

00:19:04.110 --> 00:19:05.450
That's blatant favoritism!

00:19:05.450 --> 00:19:06.370
Yeah.

00:19:06.370 --> 00:19:07.980
I feel the same way.

00:19:07.980 --> 00:19:09.360
Should we protest?

00:19:10.760 --> 00:19:12.790
Oh, you're both out early.

00:19:18.080 --> 00:19:20.470
Combined practice was fun, wasn't it?

00:19:20.470 --> 00:19:21.930
Everyone was so amazing.

00:19:23.690 --> 00:19:24.900
Is something wrong?

00:19:27.150 --> 00:19:28.420
Hey.

00:19:28.420 --> 00:19:30.940
Do you know what's pissing me off about you?

00:19:38.150 --> 00:19:39.950
What are you mad about?

00:19:40.600 --> 00:19:41.200
That right there!

00:19:44.610 --> 00:19:47.700
Those puppy dog eyes are what's pissing me off!

00:19:48.140 --> 00:19:51.750
Those eyes that just scream that you love diving so much, you can't even help it.

00:19:52.580 --> 00:19:55.460
How we should all just "do our best"!

00:19:57.280 --> 00:19:59.460
That's a fairy tale.

00:20:00.290 --> 00:20:04.720
I hope you don't think athletes are all happy and supportive people.

00:20:05.450 --> 00:20:07.870
That's just a lie. A big fat lie.

00:20:08.520 --> 00:20:10.390
Everyone's selfish and greedy.

00:20:10.390 --> 00:20:12.810
They aren't satisfied unless they're number one.

00:20:13.750 --> 00:20:16.650
That's why everyone jealously looks at each other like rivals.

00:20:17.520 --> 00:20:20.400
Everyone has these feelings inside them!

00:20:22.290 --> 00:20:23.990
That's enough, Ryou.

00:20:24.510 --> 00:20:29.330
It's always the idiot who says it's all about
friendship who wins in the manga and movies.

00:20:52.060 --> 00:20:53.220
<i>I thought...</i>

00:20:54.090 --> 00:20:58.020
<i>I thought I really enjoyed diving.</i>

00:20:59.640 --> 00:21:04.050
<i>That's why I couldn't understand Ryou's sudden outburst.</i>

00:21:04.910 --> 00:21:07.030
<i>I couldn't understand what I did wrong.</i>

00:21:08.110 --> 00:21:10.040
<i>I didn't understand anything.</i>

00:21:11.720 --> 00:21:15.150
<i>The diving that I'd loved so much</i>

00:21:16.430 --> 00:21:20.050
<i>was now causing me so much pain.</i>
